232
00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:12.000
So, you have to be specific,

233
00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:15.000
even if you don't place an intention.

234
00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:18.000
I think it's terribly important to place an intention.

235
00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:23.000
In the order of grace, it happens in the same way as the natural order.

236
00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.000
In other words, you've got to be very specific.

237
00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:28.000
The sun gives light to everyone,

238
00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:31.000
and yet not everyone enjoys the same effects,

239
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.000
because some people go out and bathe in the sunlight.

240
00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:38.000
Other people hide and pull the curtains.

241
00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.000
So, the ones who hide and pull the curtains

242
00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:45.000
are not going to get the same benefits as the ones get in the sunburn.

243
00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:48.000
However, this is not because of the sun.

244
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.000
It's because of our decision.

245
00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.000
One uses the light of the sun in order to work,

246
00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:56.000
to be industrious, to learn, to appreciate things.

247
00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:59.000
And this one makes herself rich.

248
00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:05.000
She constitutes herself and does not go around begging for bread from others.

249
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:09.000
Someone else keeps lazing about,

250
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.000
these are the ones that only want sunburn,

251
00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.000
but they don't want anything else.

252
00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.000
And she does not want to meddle in anything.

253
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.000
The light of the sun inundates her everywhere,

254
00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:21.000
but for her it's useless.

255
00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.000
She wants to do nothing with it.

256
00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:29.000
Now, those of us who are teachers know it's very fascinating.

257
00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.000
I've noticed it on a secondary school level,

258
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.000
even more particularly at a primary school level,

259
00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:38.000
when the sun shines, the children are all energy.

260
00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.000
I want to get up and do stuff.

261
00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:45.000
And if it's raining, they lose the motivation to actually work.

262
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:51.000
And so the sunlight actually energizes them to do stuff.

263
00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:56.000
But if the sunlight makes us lazy, we're in trouble.

264
00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.000
So the second one keeps lazing about,

265
00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:01.000
okay, she doesn't want to meddle in anything.

266
00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:03.000
The light of the sun inundates her everywhere,

267
00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:07.000
but for her it's useless, and she wants to do nothing with it.

268
00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:09.000
So there's the lazy bones.

269
00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:15.000
This one is poor and sickly because a sloth produces many evils.

270
00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:19.000
Now sloth is one of the deadly sins.

271
00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:22.000
Sloth is one of the deadly sins.

272
00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:26.000
It produces many evils, physical and moral.

273
00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:30.000
And if she feels hungry, she needs to beg for someone else's bread,

274
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.000
because she's too lazy to do someone about it herself.

275
00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:37.000
Now, is the light of the sun perhaps responsible for these two,

276
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.000
or does it give more to one than to the other?

277
00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.000
Certainly not.

278
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:45.000
Now, when I was reading this, I thought of the ten virgins.

279
00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.000
Do you remember?

280
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:51.000
So Matthew 25, 1 to 13.

281
00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:55.000
Matthew 25, 1 to 13.

282
00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.000
Some of them are too lazy to get the oil.

283
00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:01.000
I wanted to get it from the others in the end.

284
00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:04.000
So Jesus says there's no difference between them.

285
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:08.000
The only difference is that one takes advantage of the light

286
00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.000
in a special way and the other one does not.

287
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:17.000
So that's Matthew 24, 41.

288
00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.000
Now, the same happens in the order of grace,

289
00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:23.000
which more than light inundates souls.

290
00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:28.000
At one point, it makes itself all voice to call them,

291
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.000
voice to instruct them and to correct them.

292
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:35.000
At other times, it makes itself fire and burns away from them

293
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.000
the things of down here.

294
00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.000
Down here is the earth.

295
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.000
Okay?

296
00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.000
The low level.

297
00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:47.000
That's the earth.

298
00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:51.000
And with its flames, it puts to flight creatures and pleasures from them.

299
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.000
That's the stripping.

300
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:57.000
When the Lord allows stripping, that is that something He allows

301
00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:01.000
trials and difficulties to get you to free yourself

302
00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.000
from things you're attached to.

303
00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:07.000
And with its burns, it forms pains and crosses

304
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:12.000
in order to give to the soul the shape of sanctity it wants from her.

305
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:17.000
Now, notice that whether the grace is light and beauty

306
00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:20.000
or whether it's crosses and pain,

307
00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:24.000
it's the same gift that's coming from God

308
00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:28.000
as infinite love because both are to produce sanctity.

309
00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:33.000
Okay, so sometimes you need one and sometimes you need another.

310
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:36.000
Sometimes grace makes itself water.

311
00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.000
This is number three.

312
00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:40.000
Now, number one was voice.

313
00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:44.000
Number two is fire and number three is water.

314
00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:48.000
Sometimes it makes itself water and purifies her,

315
00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:52.000
embellishes her and impregnates her completely with grace.

316
00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:56.000
But who is attentive on receiving all of these flows of grace?

317
00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Who responds to me?

318
00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:01.000
And Jesus said, "Ah, very few."

319
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.000
And then some dare to say that to these I give grace

320
00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:09.000
for them to make themselves saints and to others I do not.

321
00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:12.000
Almost wanting to hold me responsible

322
00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:15.000
while they content themselves with conducting their lives

323
00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:18.000
lazing about as if the light of grace were not there for them.

324
00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.000
It's not wonderful.

325
00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:27.000
Matthew 25, 29.

326
00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:29.000
You did not give bread to the hungry.

327
00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:31.000
You did not, you did not, you did not, you did not.

328
00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:34.000
You laid his own souls. Okay.

329
00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:40.000
So, then he added, "My daughter, I love the soul so much

330
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:46.000
that I myself have placed myself as sentry of each heart

331
00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:51.000
to watch them, to defend them, and to work their sanctification

332
00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.000
with my own hands."

333
00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:55.000
Ephesians 2, 10.

334
00:22:55.000 --> 00:23:02.000
We are God's work of art. Ephesians 2, 10.

335
00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:06.000
Now, if you just take that sentence by itself,

336
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:11.000
there's no such a thing as coincidence.

337
00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:14.000
There's no such a thing as sort of accident.

338
00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:18.000
No matter who is responsible for what happens to you,

339
00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:23.000
God is working within you for your sanctification.

340
00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:25.000
Okay.

341
00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:28.000
And no matter whether it's a trial or a difficulty

342
00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:32.000
or it's something pleasant, it doesn't actually matter what it is,

343
00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:36.000
God wants it for you to actually grow in holiness.

344
00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:40.000
And if we get that, life will become an awful lot simpler for us.

345
00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:44.000
Instead of saying, "So-and-so is responsible for this,

346
00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:48.000
and so-and-so is responsible for that."

347
00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:52.000
So he says, "I work their sanctification with my own hands.

348
00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:54.000
I think that's beautiful."

349
00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:59.000
So the shepherd is personally involved with the sheep.

350
00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.000
Okay. So I want to give you Sam 23 for that.

351
00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:05.000
"The Lord is my shepherd. There is nothing I shall want.

352
00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:08.000
He takes care of everything."

353
00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:12.000
But how much bitterness do they not subject me to?

354
00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:17.000
Some reject me, and some don't care about me and despise me,

355
00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:20.000
and some lament about my surveillance.

356
00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:22.000
I love that.

357
00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:25.000
I want to give you Sam 139 for that.

358
00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:29.000
"Lord, you know my thoughts before I think them and my words before I say them,

359
00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:33.000
but of course if you don't love God and you want to live a very selfish life,

360
00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:36.000
you'll think of him as big brother is watching you."

361
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.000
You know what I mean?

362
00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:41.000
Some lament about my surveillance, some slam the door in my face,

363
00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:47.000
rendering my work useless because the human will has the casting vote.

364
00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:53.000
And I had not only placed myself to act as sentry,

365
00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:58.000
but on purpose do I choose the souls who live in my will.

366
00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:04.000
Please will you put a huge colored marker on that.

367
00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:09.000
You are chosen to live in the divine will.

368
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:13.000
I hope that makes you feel better.

369
00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:14.000
Does it?

370
00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:19.000
Because we're aware of our struggles and our difficulties and our this and that's not the other.

371
00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:24.000
And if you could realize that you were chosen for this,

372
00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:30.000
then the sheer privilege of it would make you move on.

373
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:35.000
But on purpose do I choose souls to live in my will.

374
00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:42.000
In fact, since they are present in all of me, that's humanity, divinity and will.

375
00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:47.000
I usually simplify that and I say, "Lord, I want to fuse all of me and all of you."

376
00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:50.000
Just to be simple about it.

377
00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:56.000
I place them with me as a second century of each heart.

378
00:25:56.000 --> 00:26:02.000
Now, the statement there is absolutely massive.

379
00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:04.000
He is the sentry of our hearth.

380
00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:07.000
We live fused in him.

381
00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:09.000
In him we find all souls.

382
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:15.000
So he said, "I place them as sentry, second century in all souls."

383
00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:19.000
In other words, you have to do the intercession that these souls are saved.

384
00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:22.000
That you've got to take care of them.

385
00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:29.000
You've got to be as detailed in wanting to love them as he is in wanting to love us.

386
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:36.000
These second centuries console me, repay me for them and keep me company

387
00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:39.000
and the loneliness into which many hearts force me.

388
00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:42.000
And they force me not to leave them.

389
00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:46.000
I think that's an absolutely astonishing statement.

390
00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:52.000
In other words, if somebody is really, really rebellious against God,

391
00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:59.000
someone like us sticks by those rebellious souls and says, "No, no, no, no.

392
00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:02.000
I'm going to keep at this. I'm going to keep at this."

393
00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:04.000
You'll get there.

394
00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:06.000
That sounds like Gregory.

395
00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:09.000
The father's really.

396
00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:11.000
Absolutely.

397
00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:17.000
Rachel who kept at Gregory for a number of years.

398
00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.000
She would not let go.

399
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:21.000
Rachel is not a real name.

400
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:24.000
It's a name we put on her meaning, "God's Beloved."

401
00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:27.000
But she kept after him and after him and after him,

402
00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:33.000
no matter how he reacted negatively or anything else and gradually she wore him down.

403
00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:36.000
And look what an incredible thing happened.

404
00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:43.000
Really, if we could only get a handle on what would happen to somebody else,

405
00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:46.000
if we don't give up.

406
00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:49.000
There's a scripture now that's just come to my mind.

407
00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:55.000
It's somewhere in Romans that St. Paul says that scripture is full of examples

408
00:27:55.000 --> 00:28:02.000
of how God helps those who refuse to give up, full of examples.

409
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:07.000
These souls chosen in the divine will are their second centuries

410
00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:12.000
and they console me, they repay me for them, for the other souls.

411
00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:15.000
They keep me company and the loneliness into which many hearts force me

412
00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:17.000
and they force me not to leave them.

413
00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:19.000
Watch this.

414
00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:23.000
I have this in two colors to make sure that I understand.

415
00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:27.000
Greater grace I could not give to souls.

416
00:28:27.000 --> 00:28:35.000
By giving them these souls who live in my will and who are the portent of portents.

417
00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:41.000
God couldn't give a greater gift to all the people on earth than people living in the divine will.

418
00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:45.000
Isn't that something?

419
00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:52.000
So I think that's so important. I've given it two colors.

420
00:28:52.000 --> 00:29:00.000
So October the 30th, 1916, we have threats of scourges in Italy.

421
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:06.000
Louisa said, I was lamenting with my beloved Jesus for in these past days he would hardly come

422
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:11.000
and I would just barely perceive his shadow and then he would disappear.

423
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:15.000
And blessed Jesus told me, my daughter, how quickly you forget

424
00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:20.000
that on those days in which I do not come so much and I escape you

425
00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:26.000
it's for nothing else but to give one more winding to the scourge.

426
00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:35.000
So there's your Amos 3 7 again that God tells the prophet ahead of time.

427
00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:40.000
Now we're in the middle of World War I, 1914 to 1918.

428
00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:45.000
And so Jesus said, things will rage more and more.

429
00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:52.000
"A man has reached such perversity," he said, "that it's not enough to touch his flesh to make him surrender.

430
00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:56.000
But I have to come to the point of pulverizing him."

431
00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:58.000
Isn't that absolutely amazing?

432
00:29:58.000 --> 00:30:04.000
So I want to give you Revelation 9 verses 20 and 21.

433
00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:09.000
Revelation 9.

434
00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:15.000
"Therefore," he said, "one nation will invade another and they will lacerate each other.

435
00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:17.000
Blood will flow like water in the towns."

436
00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:21.000
They said it was the war to end all wars and they would have ended nothing.

437
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:25.000
Even more in certain towns they will become the enemies of themselves

438
00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:27.000
and they'll fight one another.

439
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:30.000
In other words, civil war.

440
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:37.000
They will kill one another and they will do things as though crazy.

441
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:40.000
"How much man grieves me, I myself cry over him."

442
00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:44.000
At the words of Jesus I burst into crying, Louisa said,

443
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:46.000
and I prayed him to spare poor Italy.

444
00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:49.000
But Jesus continued, Italy, Italy.

445
00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:55.000
And if you knew how much evil she is up to, how many plots against my church.

446
00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:59.000
The blood she is causing to be shed in battle is not enough for her.

447
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.000
She's thirsty for more blood.

448
00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:07.000
But once the blood of my children and the blood of the primate,

449
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:10.000
in other words, she wants the pope.

450
00:31:10.000 --> 00:31:14.000
My children, of course, are members of the church.

451
00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:18.000
She wants to stay in herself with such crimes as to draw upon herself

452
00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:21.000
the revenge of heaven and of other nations.

453
00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:23.000
Notice the end.

454
00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:26.000
I remain terrorized, Louisa said.

455
00:31:26.000 --> 00:31:30.000
I fear greatly, but I hope that the Lord will placate himself.

456
00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:33.000
She doesn't say, "I hope Italy will change."

457
00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:35.000
Isn't it amazing?

458
00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:42.000
So, November the 15th, 1916, the soul forms her paradise on earth.

459
00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:44.000
You need to put a VIP beside that.

460
00:31:44.000 --> 00:31:50.000
In other words, you're responsible for whether you get to heaven or not

461
00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:55.000
and how big your palace is in heaven.

462
00:31:55.000 --> 00:32:03.000
Now, St. Paul is quite clear on this in 1 Corinthians 3 verses 11 to 15.

463
00:32:03.000 --> 00:32:09.000
And he says that on earth you decide yourself with your own actions

464
00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:13.000
whether you're going to live in a tent in heaven or a palace.

465
00:32:13.000 --> 00:32:19.000
And you decide by your actions on earth whether your tent is going to be made of cloth,

466
00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:24.000
wood or metals or gems or whatever.

467
00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:30.000
And he says, "The cloth and the wood and the grass won't survive the fire."

468
00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:33.000
In other words, we're all tested by fire.

469
00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:38.000
Okay, so we're really responsible for what we have on the other side.

470
00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:46.000
You know the joke they tell about a bus driver and a priest died on the same day

471
00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:50.000
in the same hour and arrived in heaven at the same time.

472
00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:56.000
Okay, and so St. Peter decided that he would bring both of them to their destination.

473
00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:59.000
And he said to the priest, "I hope you don't mind now.

474
00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:02.000
We're going to bring the bus driver to his palace first."

475
00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:04.000
And he got a wonderful big palace.

476
00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:09.000
You see, the priest thought, "No, I must be going to get something great."

477
00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:12.000
And then he was brought down the street and he was given a tiny little house.

478
00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:18.000
And he said to Peter, "Look, I know you're not supposed to complain in heaven or anything."

479
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:22.000
But can you explain what did he do?

480
00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:25.000
I said, "Mass, every day of my life I gave the circle.

481
00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:28.000
I taught the people. I blah, blah, blah, blah, blah."

482
00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:33.000
And he said, "Father, when you gave your sermons, they all slept.

483
00:33:33.000 --> 00:33:37.000
When he drove his bus, they all prayed."

484
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:48.000
[laughter]

485
00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:51.000
You get different palaces in heaven.

486
00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:59.000
I loved that because it's not the answer you're expecting, is it?

487
00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:03.000
So here's November the 15th, 1916.

488
00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:09.000
Louisa said, "I was lamenting to my sweet Jesus that he no longer loved me as before.

489
00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:11.000
She loves going on like that."

490
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:17.000
So he said, "My daughter, not loving one who loves me is impossible for me.

491
00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:18.000
God is love."

492
00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:20.000
One, John, four, seven.

493
00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:23.000
That's his nature.

494
00:34:23.000 --> 00:34:25.000
Okay.

495
00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:36.000
And Sam 1, 4, 5, verse 17, "God only ever acts out of love."

496
00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:43.000
So Jesus said, "Rather, I feel so drawn to her that at the littlest act of love that

497
00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:46.000
she does for me, notice littlest."

498
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.000
He's not looking for great things.

499
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:55.000
"I respond with triple love, why triple love, Father, Son, and Holy Spirit."

500
00:34:55.000 --> 00:34:58.000
Okay.

501
00:34:58.000 --> 00:35:07.000
"And I place a divine vein in her heart which administers to her divine knowledge,

502
00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:10.000
divine sanctity, and divine virtue."

503
00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:12.000
Now notice this vein.

504
00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:18.000
That's like saying that the doctor has inserted a tube into you which is feeding you

505
00:35:18.000 --> 00:35:21.000
the stuff that you need to receive.

506
00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:26.000
And this divine vein is giving divine knowledge, divine sanctity, and divine virtue.

507
00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:29.000
Now it's divine knowledge that we need.

508
00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:31.000
We've lots of human knowledge.

509
00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:34.000
It's divine sanctity that we need.

510
00:35:34.000 --> 00:35:36.000
We have ordinary holiness.

511
00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.000
Okay.

512
00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:39.000
And it's divine virtue.

513
00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:44.000
"The more the soul loves me, the more this divine vein rises,

514
00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:49.000
and watering all the powers of the soul, intellect, memory, and will,

515
00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:51.000
the powers of the soul.

516
00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:55.000
It diffuses for the good of the other souls.

517
00:35:55.000 --> 00:36:01.000
"I've placed this vein in you," he said, "and when you lack my presence

518
00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:05.000
and do not hear my voice, this vein will make up for everything

519
00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:09.000
and will be the voice for you and for the other creatures."

520
00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:12.000
So that's that message complete.

521
00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:17.000
On another day, Louisa was fusing all of herself as usual

522
00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:19.000
in the divine and blessed Jesus.

523
00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:26.000
And he said to her, "My daughter, the more you fuse yourself in me,

524
00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:29.000
the more I fuse myself in you.

525
00:36:29.000 --> 00:36:32.000
Would you put a big, big marker on that one?"

526
00:36:32.000 --> 00:36:37.000
And do it as frequently as you can.

527
00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:44.000
So it is on earth that the soul forms her paradise.

528
00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:49.000
According to how much she fills herself with holy thoughts,

529
00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:53.000
with holy affections, with holy desires, with holy words,

530
00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:57.000
with holy works and steps, so does she keep forming her paradise.

531
00:36:57.000 --> 00:37:03.000
So these are all the bricks to make your palace.

532
00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:09.000
To one more holy thought or word, one more contentment will correspond

533
00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:16.000
at the many varieties of beauty, contentment, glory, for as much good as she has done.

534
00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:23.000
1 Corinthians 3, 10 to 15.

535
00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:29.000
What will the surprise of this soul be when, once the prison of her body is broken,

536
00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:34.000
immediately, she will find herself in the sea of as many pleasures and happiness

537
00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:41.000
as much light and beauty for as much good that she has done even for a thought?

538
00:37:41.000 --> 00:37:44.000
Isn't that fantastic?

539
00:37:44.000 --> 00:37:56.000
So, let's do November the 30th, 1916, the benefits of repairing for others.

540
00:37:56.000 --> 00:38:00.000
Jesus said I was very afflicted because of the privation of my adorable Jesus,

541
00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.000
and I cried bitterly.

542
00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:06.000
And as I was doing the hours of the Passion, a thought tormented me, saying to me,

543
00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:11.000
"Look at what good your reparations for others have done to you."

544
00:38:11.000 --> 00:38:16.000
They've caused you to let Jesus escape you, and much more nonsense, that is nonsense.

545
00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:19.000
Why? Because he's within her all the time.

546
00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:26.000
The Blessed Jesus was moved at compassion, and he said, "My daughter, you are my goad.

547
00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:30.000
My love is cornered by your violences."

548
00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:32.000
You don't need the "s."

549
00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:41.000
Matthew 11, 12, says that the Kingdom of God suffers violence, and the violent take it by force.

550
00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:44.000
Now, some people are just too lazy to become saints.

551
00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:50.000
They wouldn't be bothered paying the price, so they don't become saints.

552
00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:57.000
If you knew how much I suffer in seeing you suffer because of me,

553
00:38:57.000 --> 00:39:05.000
it is justice that wants to pour itself out, and your very violence forces me to hide.

554
00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:09.000
Things will rage more, therefore you have to have patience.

555
00:39:09.000 --> 00:39:17.000
Besides, know that the reparations done for others have done great good to you.

556
00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:22.000
Now, that's not what you're expecting, is it?

557
00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:31.000
Because in repairing for others, you intended to do what I did, and I repaired for all, therefore you're included.

558
00:39:31.000 --> 00:39:35.000
If you pray for all souls past, present, and future, you actually are one of them.

559
00:39:35.000 --> 00:39:43.000
If you pray for all the dying past, present, and future, then you are prayed for in your dying, even if nobody else prayed.

560
00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:47.000
See the logic that he's using.

561
00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:51.000
So, it also, you're repaired for you.

562
00:39:51.000 --> 00:39:57.000
I asked forgiveness for all, I grieved for the offenses of all, and I asked forgiveness for you.

563
00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:59.000
And for you also, I grieved.

564
00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:06.000
Therefore, as you did what I did, you also take the reparations for forgiveness and sorrow that I had for you.

565
00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:13.000
So, what could be more good for you than my reparations, my forgiveness, and my sorrow?

566
00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:16.000
Mine are yours.

567
00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:21.000
And then he said, "I never let myself be surpassed in love.

568
00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:28.000
When I see that for love of me, the soul is all intent on repairing me, loving me, apologizing to me,

569
00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:30.000
and asking forgiveness for sinners.

570
00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:35.000
To give her tit for tat, I ask forgiveness for her in a special way."

571
00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:40.000
Now, I don't know about you, but I would underline that about three times.

572
00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:41.000
Okay.

573
00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:50.000
"And I repair for love of her, and I keep embellishing her soul with my love, with my reparations and my forgiveness,

574
00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:56.000
therefore continue to repair and do not raise conflicts between you and me."

575
00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:57.000
Isn't that a nice message?

576
00:40:57.000 --> 00:41:00.600
You have a nice message, okay, so I'm going to leave it there for tonight.
